  "notes": [
    "Regional site overlay (ADR 0042) for an Estonian cluster village in northern Harria in April 1343, before St George's Night: five farmsteads round a common, smoke saunas by a brook, open strip fields, a wet meadow, a fenced common pasture and woods to the south toward the Pirita valley.",
    "Invented composite (docs/LOCATIONS/harju_village.md, history/dossiers/hinterland/harju-village-and-manor.md): no surveyed 1343 village. The terrain is EU-DEM at Rebala (Joelahtme parish), a representative limestone-plateau village of the Iru-Rebala-Joelahtme corridor east of Reval, chosen for the game; the village is not Rebala and claims nothing about it. Coordinates are metres from that origin, x east, y south.",
    "Farmsteads are barn-dwellings (rehielamu: smoke room and threshing floor under one thatch) with a granary and a shed; no chimneys (smoke leaves through the gable). Points of interest of kind smoke carry the plume height for the site script (scenes/world/sites/hinterland_site.gd).",
    "OSM supplies nothing to the plan (land cover only, for the record); no modern road, building or pond is used."
  ],
